---
title: Arugula Salad with Feta
description: Crisp, peppery arugula tossed with sweet cherry tomatoes, crumbled Greek feta, and a bright honey-mustard white balsamic vinaigrette.
servings: 2
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 5 minutes
tags:
  - salads
  - vegetarian
  - quick
  - mediterranean
source: https://www.gaumenfreundin.de/rucola-salat/#rezept
---

= Prepare Greens & Tomatoes

Wash and dry @arugula{125%g} thoroughly (using a #salad spinner{} so the dressing clings properly).

Slice @cherry tomatoes{250%g} into halves.

= Whisk Dressing

In a #small mixing bowl{} (or small lidded #jar{}), whisk together @extra virgin olive oil{4%tbsp}, @white balsamic vinegar{2%tbsp}, @Dijon mustard{1%tsp}, and @honey{1%tsp}.

Season with @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp} and freshly ground @black pepper{1/4%tsp}, whisking vigorously with a #small whisk{} or fork until smooth and emulsified.

= Assemble & Toss

In a #large salad bowl{}, combine the dried @arugula{}, halved @cherry tomatoes{}, and crumbled @feta{150%g}.

Drizzle the vinaigrette evenly over the salad. Toss gently to coat without bruising the tender leaves, and serve immediately.
